      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_nono2ratio"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "chain"
        ],
        "note": "333 rows: the species-over-NOx multiplier for each (polProcessID, sourceTypeID, fuelTypeID, modelYearGroupID). Unlike `pm10emissionratio`, which carries an inclusive model-year BAND, this table is keyed by a model-year GROUP and needs `pollutantprocessmappedmodelyear` to say which years the group covers -- the same expansion `NOCalculator.sql`'s NOCalculation1 performs. Source type 21 carries 37 groups per (species, fuel type) over fuel types 1, 2 and 5 and NONE for fuel type 9, which is why electricity is absent from all three species blocks. The three ratios sum to exactly 1 within a (fuel type, group) cell -- 0.932 + 0.060 + 0.008 for gasoline, 0.96224 + 0.02976 + 0.008 for diesel -- so a document that swapped NO and NO2 would still conserve mass and only the per-cell check would see it.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
