        "tags": [
          "adjustment"
        ],
        "note": "3 rows, one per combusting fuel type. The NOx humidity correction `k`, and the only table in this repository whose EQUATION is a text column: fuel types 1 and 5 use `CFR 86` (a linear correction on bounded specific humidity in g/kg) and fuel type 2 uses `CFR 1065` (a reciprocal correction on bounded water mole fraction). Both branches fire in this run. `humidityTermB` is NULL on the CFR 86 rows, so it is read inside an aggregate FILTERED to CFR 1065 and its NaN never reaches an arithmetic operator. Fuel type 9 has no row at all and takes adjust.rs:521's `nha.map_or(1.0, ...)`.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    }
  },
