    "n_outputRate": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 436,
      "description": "THE ONE DECLARED NUMBER IN THIS DOCUMENT: how many (pollutant-process, cohort) pairs reach MOVESOutput per day type. Total NOx emits 124 of the 164 candidates -- 41 gasoline model years, 40 diesel, 23 E85 and 20 electricity -- and each of the three species emits 104, because `nono2ratio` has no fuel type 9 row and the whole electricity column drops out of the chain. 124 + 3 x 104 = 436, and 436 x 2 day types is the snapshot's 872. NONE of that raggedness is written down: `rt_survives` is the mask and `rt_prefixSurvives` an inclusive prefix count over the pollutant-process-major rate relation that numbers the survivors 1..436 across ALL blocks at once -- docs/esm-conventions.md 22, and the same shape docs/process-refueling.md 3.3 uses for its 64 + 104. `rateSurvivorCount` recomputes 436 from the chain and `pp_rateCohortCount` recomputes 124/104/104/104 separately per pollutant-process; the tests pin all of them."
    },
    "n_runspecpollutantprocess": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in runspecpollutantprocess. The FIRST factor of the rate relation -- four pollutant-processes here -- and, through the rate relation's survival mask, the first factor of the output relation too. A run selecting one more would size both differently with no other edit."
    },
