        "cty_barometricPressure": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "inHg",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "county_rows"
          ],
          "description": "county.barometricPressure, 29.095 inches of mercury. The unit is declared: `inHg` entered the registry at exactly 25.4 mmHg with EarthSciAST `fa7ffb01e`, retiring finding F34. Every use multiplies by 3.38639 to reach kPa, once, in lib/meteorology.esm's `ambient_pressure_kilopascals`.\n\nWHAT IS NOT CARRIED, AND WHY. MOVES runs two `UPDATE County` statements before the humidity pass: MG-1 fills a missing or non-positive pressure from the altitude CLASS, and MG-2 then classes a missing altitude from the pressure MG-1 has just written. Neither is carried here. MG-1's guard cannot fire on this snapshot -- measured across all 40 snapshots in the corpus, 22,815 `County` rows, not one has a NULL or non-positive `barometricPressure` (docs/meteorology-generator.md 8.1) -- and carrying it anyway would require `County.altitude`, a single-character TEXT column no `float_columns` can deliver, so the fixture would have to WRITE THE ALTITUDE CLASS DOWN as a constant transcribed from the reference table, which is the one thing a fixture exists not to do. MG-2 writes a column nothing downstream in this repository reads. Both fallback arms are checked instead in components/meteorology.esm, county rows 3 to 5, against the SQL as ported -- and docs/meteorology-generator.md 8.1 says plainly that the corpus cannot check them against MOVES at all.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "nox_county",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "barometricPressure"
            }
          }
        },
        "rgc_regionID": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
