      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "the_run_scope_comes_from_the_execution_database",
          "description": "Year 2020, August, hour 7, source type 21, road type 4, county 26161, zone 261610. The RunSpec XML says month 7 and hour 6; the execution database says 8 and 7, and it is the authority (docs/mixed-onroad.md 0.1). The last four rows are what this fixture adds to that list: at 59.5 degF the hour also carries 10.0536843 g/kg of specific humidity and a 0.0159290590 water mole fraction, and the county carries a GPA fraction of 0 -- the humidity pair drives the whole NOx temperature factor and the GPA fraction selects which arm of every fuel effect applies.\n\nTHE TWO HUMIDITY ROWS FACE THE REFERENCE ACROSS THIS DOCUMENT'S OWN ARITHMETIC (docs/esm-conventions.md 35.4). Their `expected` is what `ZoneMonthHour` STORES; since docs/meteorology-generator.md 8.2 the value under test is not that column but MG-4 to MG-7 run here from `temperature`, `relHumidity` and `County.barometricPressure`. Measured, the port lands 10.053684062398 against the stored 10.053684293477 (2.2985e-08 relative) and 0.015929058669 against 0.015929059029 (2.2619e-08). Those two rows therefore carry `rel: 1e-7` -- four times the worse of the pair, the same gate components/meteorology.esm asserts the whole generator at, and 200x tighter than tolerance.toml's per-cell 2e-05. The other sixteen rows are keys and stay at the test's exact 1e-09.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "tolerance": {
            "rel": 1e-09
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "run_yearID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 2020.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_monthID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 8.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_hourID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 7.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_sourceTypeID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 21.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_roadTypeID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 4.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_countyID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 26161.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_zoneID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 261610.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_stateID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 26.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_baseYearIsAnalysisYear",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_fuelYearID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 2020.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_hpmsVtypeID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 25.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_daysInMonth",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 31.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_monthGroupID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 8.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_temperature",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 59.5,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_heatIndex",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 59.5,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_specificHumidity",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 10.053684293477,
              "tolerance": {
                "rel": 1e-7
              },
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_molWaterFraction",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.015929059029,
              "tolerance": {
                "rel": 1e-7
              },
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "run_gpaFraction",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "the_four_pollutant_processes_and_the_three_chains",
          "description": "The run's whole pollutant scope, unpacked from `runspecpollutantprocess` and `runspecchainedto` rather than written down. 301 is Oxides of Nitrogen x Running Exhaust and is the only one with rates of its own; 3201, 3301 and 3401 are NO, NO2 and HONO on the same process and each is chained from 301. `calculator-dag.json` splits them between two Java classes -- `NOCalculator` registers (32, 1) and (34, 1), `NO2Calculator` registers (33, 1) -- and the split is invisible here on purpose: both classes' SQL 'Processing' sections are the same two joins and the same multiply, so one chain expression serves all three. None of the four is an energy pollutant, so every unit divisor is exactly 1 and `baserateunits` says `g` four times.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "rspp_pollutantID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 3.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_pollutantID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 32.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 2
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_pollutantID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 33.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 3
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_pollutantID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 34.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 4
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_processID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_processID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 2
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_processID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 3
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_processID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 4
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_isEnergy",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_isEnergy",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 4
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_unitDivisor",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_unitDivisor",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 2
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_unitDivisor",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 3
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_unitDivisor",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 4
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_chainInputPolProcessID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "rspp_chainInputPolProcessID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 301.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecpollutantprocess_rows": 2
