        {
          "id": "the_criteria_fuel_effect_is_market_share_weighted_over_the_supplied_formulations",
          "description": "The fuel effect, which no fixture before this one had. `fuelsupply` offers five formulations; four resolve to a fuel type this run selects (90 -> subtype 90 -> electricity, 9114 -> 12 -> gasoline, 25003 -> 21 -> diesel, 27002 -> 51 -> E85) and the fifth carries subtype 30, which `fuelsubtype` does not have, so it resolves to fuel type 0 and joins no cohort. All five are in the county's region and in the run's fuel year and month group, so `fsu_isSupplied` is 1 on all five and the drop is done by the resolution and not by the mask.\\n\\nThe factors are `criteriaratio.ratio` blended with `ratioGPA` at a GPA fraction of 0, so they are the normal arm exactly: 0.927694995111 for gasoline model year 2020 and for E85 model year 2020 (both formulations carry the same ETOH and aromatic content), 0.962413415319 for gasoline 1980, 1.00385 for diesel 1980. Diesel 2019 and E85 1998 have NO row -- the table stops at 2006 for 25003 and starts at 2001 for 27002 -- and take 1 rather than 0, which is the difference between a missing effect and a fatal one. So do all three species, whose polProcessID `criteriaratio` does not carry.",
